<title>UK: Bankers Trust sets warrants on Chinese shares.</title>
<headline>Bankers Trust sets warrants on Chinese shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankers Trust International Plc says it has issued two million American-style call warrants, on a basket of China B shares comprising Shanghai Refrigerator Compressor, Shanghai Lujiazui Finance &amp; Trade, Inner Mongolia Erdos Cashmere Products, Guangdong Electric Power</p>
<p>Development Co, Hefei Meiling Co and China Merchants</p>
<p>Shekou Port.</p>
<p>One warrant controls one unit of the basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE    $4.6682		   PREMIUM	19.30 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE     $1.52		     GEARING	3.39 TIMES</p>
<p> EXERCISE PERIOD 16.DEC.96-21.NOV.97   PAYDATE	13.DEC.96</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG		MIN EXER LOT =</p>
<p>SPOT REFERENCE  $5.1869 --Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
